          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8109133738d4b5ef86b5691ff0429ade42470959e9fdbabca622a873fb0c7662:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7c6e888d3db141d58fd798ac6f70716f",
      "statement": "The component's root-adjustment and feature-read-back surface is unimplemented and is kept explicit because it is the contract the crowd and collision control inputs were written against; finishing it means routing to the Transform and to the matching stage's query vector rather than adding state, since both facts already have owners. Only the four methods throw NotImplementedException — the four Root properties silently return default.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L369-L406",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:75b2e1478f9040d1ee340e4389a83831b3fb111c78585605742dbcc7a00bcd5a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_86fdcc7cb22443f7a389ad0a1459ed66",
      "statement": "Inertialized hips blending across a rootPositionsMask change and toe-floor penetration correction were dropped when the pipeline moved to stages, and the intended home for each is a MoSynthStage running after the pose is produced rather than another special case inside the orchestrator.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L344-L348",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:accd251de68f2ca8bfe0fd3911cfab5e64ffed0a021aa53f4a48f7fc198ea998:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f8435de4b3c04b4ca85258a3ce3063d2",
      "statement": "Advancing the character's Transform by the frame's own velocity is gated on the rootPositionsMask flag; when it is off the pose is still applied and bone 0 is still placed frame-locally, but the Transform is never integrated, so the character animates in place instead of travelling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L308-L342",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77ef9ae8431ee8ea6e23613a769bf9f2e5861c0dc61df906312e6c61bbbdcdc9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e3792819d674407b9f33ff865df7a0ab",
      "statement": "Applying a pose writes bone 0's local position and rotation but writes only the local rotation of every other bone — their local positions are never touched — so bone lengths come from the scene rig's own Transforms rather than from the pose.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L308-L342",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77ef9ae8431ee8ea6e23613a769bf9f2e5861c0dc61df906312e6c61bbbdcdc9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_676ef2fbbb2d40d38176ed4764b8dfe2",
      "statement": "The seeded per-tick velocity delta is consumed downstream as though it were a per-second rate and multiplied by the timestep again, and the Euler-degrees angular channel is fed to a scaled-angle-axis conversion that expects radians, so both errors compound rather than cancelling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L273-L292",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e01933f77bfa6ed2b73f9942e13e77143438dce83206e959e3038ecbc90f8bf:"
        },
